# The only image built from the repository root is the cloud runner
# (`runner/Dockerfile`); the API and the worker are built from `server/` and
# read `server/.dockerignore` instead. The runner's context is the root only
# because the engine patches live under `desktop/`, so everything else is
# excluded by hand: without this, the context would carry the git history, the
# web client, the corpus and the desktop's built OpenClaw runtime, none of
# which the image copies and all of which would be uploaded on every build.
#
# Exclude everything, then name what the Dockerfile actually copies.
*
!runner
!desktop/package.json
!desktop/scripts/apply-openclaw-patches.cjs
!desktop/scripts/patches

# ...minus what is generated inside those paths. A developer's local build
# would otherwise ship their `node_modules` into the build context and
# invalidate the runner layer on every `npm install`.
runner/node_modules
runner/dist
runner/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
